[comment {-*- tcl -*- doctools manpage}]
[vset VERSION 0.1]
[manpage_begin map::provider::osm n [vset VERSION]]
[category {Map Display and Supporting Utilities}]
[keywords map {tile provider} {provider, tiles} openstreetmap mapnik]
[moddesc   {Map display support}]
[titledesc {Tile provider using OpenStreetMap Mapnik as origin}]
[require Tcl 8.6-]
[require debug]
[require debug::caller]
[require map::slippy 0.8]
[require map::slippy::cache]
[require map::slippy::fetcher]
[require snit]
[require map::provider::osm [opt [vset VERSION]]]
[description]

This package provides a tile provider suitable for use with [package map::display], see the
section [emph {Tile provider}] of its manpage for the API every tile provider has to support.

It uses the OpenStreetMap Mapnik tile server ([uri https://tile.openstreetmap.org]) as origin and
caches fetched tiles in the local filesystem, using the packages [package map::slippy::fetcher] and
[package map::slippy::cache].

[para] As the tile server is accessed via [const https], creating a provider requires that the
[package http] package supports this protocol: either it is already registered with
[cmd http::register], or the package [package tls] (or, on Windows, [package twapi_crypto]) is
available and is used to register it.

[section {Class API}]

[list_begin definitions]
[call [cmd ::map::provider::osm] [arg objectName] [arg cachedir]]
[call [cmd {::map provider osm}] [arg objectName] [arg cachedir]]

This command creates a new tile provider named [arg objectName] and returns the fully qualified
name of the object command. The name [const %AUTO%] generates a unique name.

[para] The directory [arg cachedir] holds the cached tiles. It has to exist. The tile for zoom
level [var z], row [var r] and column [var c] is stored in the PNG file
[file [var cachedir]/[var z]/[var c]/[var r].png].
[list_end]

[section Methods]

[list_begin definitions]
[call [arg objectName] [method levels]]

This method returns the number of zoom levels supported by the provider, [const 20].

[call [arg objectName] [method tilewidth]]
[call [arg objectName] [method tileheight]]

These methods return the width and the height of the tiles, in pixels ([const 256]).

[call [arg objectName] [method get] [arg tile] [arg donecmd]]

This method requests the image of the [arg tile], a 3-element list of zoom level, row, and
column, in this order. The result of the method is the empty string.

[para] The command prefix [arg donecmd] is invoked at the global level, in one of the forms

[example {
    {*}$donecmd set   $tile $image  ;# The image for the tile is available
    {*}$donecmd unset $tile         ;# There is no image for the tile
}]

where [arg image] is the name of a new photo image showing the tile.

[para] A tile found in the cache is reported asynchronously, from the event loop. A tile not in
the cache is fetched from the tile server, stored in the cache, and then reported; a tile which
cannot be fetched is reported as [const unset]. An invalid tile
(i.e. one outside of the map at its zoom level, or with an unsupported zoom level) is reported as
[const unset] immediately, before the method returns.

[para] Errors thrown by [arg donecmd] are not propagated; their stack trace is printed to
[const stdout].

[call [arg objectName] [method destroy]]

This method destroys the provider.

[list_end]

[section EXAMPLE]

[example {
package require map::display
package require map::provider::osm

file mkdir tiles
set provider [map provider osm %AUTO% tiles]
map display .map -provider $provider -initial-geo {48.137 11.575} -initial-zoom 12
pack .map -fill both -expand 1
}]

